text:
Each `_has` condition is evaluated independently. Thus q1 includes pt-2: o-3 supplies the HbA1c code, while o-4 supplies the value above 9. The composite in q2 requires both conditions on the same Observation.

q3 still includes pt-5: o-6 satisfies the composite, and o-7 independently satisfies `status=final`. q4 requires a resolvable patient with female gender, leaving o-1 and o-5.

Includes add existing resources without filtering the matches. Thus o-8 matches q5, but its absent Patient/pt-9 cannot be included. q6 includes prov-2 once despite its two matching targets. q7 adds Observations and Provenance directly referencing the matching Patients; without iteration, it does not add Provenance targeting those included Observations.

```json
{
  "q1": ["Patient/pt-1", "Patient/pt-2", "Patient/pt-3", "Patient/pt-5"],
  "q2": ["Patient/pt-1", "Patient/pt-3", "Patient/pt-5"],
  "q3": ["Patient/pt-1", "Patient/pt-3", "Patient/pt-5"],
  "q4": ["Observation/o-1", "Observation/o-5"],
  "q5": {
    "match": ["Observation/o-1", "Observation/o-5", "Observation/o-6", "Observation/o-8"],
    "include": ["Patient/pt-1", "Patient/pt-3", "Patient/pt-5"]
  },
  "q6": {
    "match": ["Observation/o-3", "Observation/o-4"],
    "include": ["Provenance/prov-2"]
  },
  "q7": {
    "match": ["Patient/pt-1", "Patient/pt-3"],
    "include": ["Observation/o-1", "Observation/o-2", "Observation/o-5", "Provenance/prov-3"]
  }
}
```
